<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary/80 font-medium italic mb-8 border-l-4 border-secondary pl-6">Yes — orthognathic (jaw) surgery is one of the most transformative cosmetic procedures in modern surgery. It changes the underlying facial skeleton, which is what gives the face its shape and balance. Patients routinely describe the change as looking "more like themselves, only better" — balanced, defined, and harmonious.</p>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 rounded-xl border border-surface-container-high my-10 not-prose shadow-sm">
